score_pct: 27.0
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test or review comment addresses from_file_or_default swallowing all
    errors. The config tests check loading behavior but don't distinguish NotFound
    from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer verified '[VERIFIED] ServerError Display suppresses raw response\
    \ body (CWE-209)' but the actual finding is about eprintln leaking CliError Display\
    \ to stderr. However, the security_test.rs suite covers CWE-209 error exposure,\
    \ and the Dev implemented sanitized Display. Partially caught \u2014 Dev avoided\
    \ raw transparent forwarding for ServerError, but the broader CliError Display\
    \ still uses eprintln directly in main.rs. Given main.rs is a placeholder (H-1),\
    \ the full path isn't exercised. Borderline \u2014 marking caught by dev since\
    \ ServerError Display was sanitized."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: SiemClient.tenant_id is a raw String. Dev added CRLF sanitization (sanitize_header_value)
    which mitigates header injection, but the finding is about using axiathon-core's
    validated TenantId type instead of raw String. The type-safety gap was not flagged.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "Reviewer marked '[VERIFIED] Workspace dependency management \u2014 all\
    \ deps at workspace level' but the ground truth says 6 deps use direct version\
    \ strings instead of workspace = true. Reviewer missed this."
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding M-2: 'Config silently accepts unknown fields \u2014\
    \ token field ignored without warning... Add #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] to\
    \ RawConfig so users get an explicit error if they put secrets in the config file.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in the test suite. TEA wrote the tests but included this logical flaw, and
    neither Dev nor Reviewer caught it.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions (let _ = config). TEA wrote
    tests with this pattern, Dev passed them, Reviewer noted tests were 'well-structured
    with clear assertions' without catching this specific gap.
